cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LangSlice in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "LangSlice: VLM-driven registration of histological brain sections to BrainGlobe atlases"
abstract: >
  LangSlice gives a vision-language agent tools to register histological
  brain sections to BrainGlobe atlases. The agent determines positions and
  cutting angles, aligns sections in-plane, and optionally fits ANTs
  deformations to the stain or to borders traced by an image model.
  Results include coordinate and label maps, registration parameters,
  and QuickNII / VisuAlign exports, with native registration updates in ABBA.
